<div>
  <p>You can set a custom refund policy by adding it to your product settings. Digital products must offer at least a 7-day money-back guarantee. Physical products can still use a no-refunds policy. This helps your customers know what to expect and allows Gumroad Support to issue refunds on your behalf. We also include your policy in any credit card or PayPal dispute, providing an extra layer of protection for your business.</p>
  <h3>Adding a refund policy</h3>
  <p>On the product edit page, under the Settings section of the Product tab, toggle <b>Specify a refund policy for this product</b>. From here, you can pick a refund period or copy a refund period from another product to save time.</p>
  <p style="" class=""><%= image_tag "help_center/product-level-refund-policy-edit.png" %></p>
  <p>The refund period is shown on the product page.</p>
  <p>To remove the refund policy, simply switch off the toggle and save the product. </p>
